Package: portable-os-admin
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-tk, parted, cryptsetup, debootstrap
Description: Admin tool for portable LUKS-encrypted OS media
 Creates and administers an encrypted admin container, builds install
 configurations, installs Debian/Astra Linux or RedOS onto an external
 LUKS-encrypted medium, and manages its logs/exchange partition/recovery
 codes afterwards. Ships both a guided Tkinter GUI (`portable-os-admin`,
 the default) and a Textual TUI (`portable-os-admin-tui`) built on the
 same backend.
 .
 The Python dependencies this project actually needs (textual>=0.58,
 cryptography>=41.0) are newer than Debian's own packaged versions
 (python3-textual in bookworm is 0.1.13, a pre-rewrite release with a
 different widget API), so this package installs them into a private
 virtualenv at /opt/portable-os-admin/venv during configuration instead
 of depending on the system packages -- see packaging/README.md in the
 source tree for why, and what that means for offline installs. The GUI's
 own dependency, Tkinter, is the one exception: it's a C extension bound
 to the system Python (confirmed present in Debian bookworm's own
 Packages.gz as python3-tk), not installable from PyPI, so it comes from
 this Depends line and the venv is created with --system-site-packages so
 it can see it.
